{"id":"17.3.1.1","doc":"T","title":"Internal Memory","words":442,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The following registers can be used to control ESP32-S3's internal memory:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"In register "},{"t":"reg","v":"SYSCON_CLKGATE_FORCE_ON_REG"},{"t":"text","v":":"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Setting different bits of the "},{"t":"field","v":"SYSCON_ROM_CLKGATE_FORCE_ON"},{"t":"text","v":" field forces on the clock gates of different blocks of Internal ROM 0 and Internal ROM 1."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Setting different bits of the "},{"t":"field","v":"SYSCON_SRAM_CLKGATE_FORCE_ON"},{"t":"text","v":" field forces on the clock gates of different blocks of Internal SRAM."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"This means when the respective bits of this register are set to 1, the clock gate of the corresponding ROM or SRAM blocks will always be on."}]},{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Otherwise, the clock gate will turn on automatically when the corresponding ROM or SRAM blocks are accessed and turn off automatically when the corresponding ROM or SRAM blocks are not accessed."}]},{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Therefore, it's recommended to configure these bits to 0 to lower power consumption."}]}]}]]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":8,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"In register "},{"t":"reg","v":"SYSCON_MEM_POWER_DOWN_REG"},{"t":"text","v":":"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":9,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Setting different bits of the "},{"t":"field","v":"SYSCON_ROM_POWER_DOWN"},{"t":"text","v":" field sends different blocks of Internal ROM 0 and Internal ROM 1 into retention state."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":10,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Setting different bits of the "},{"t":"field","v":"SYSCON_SRAM_POWER_DOWN"},{"t":"text","v":" field sends different blocks of Internal SRAM into retention state."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":11,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The \"Retention\" state is a low-power state of a memory block."}]},{"n":12,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"In this state, the memory block still holds all the data stored but cannot be accessed, thus reducing the power consumption."}],"warn":true},{"n":13,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Therefore, you can send a certain block of memory into the retention state to reduce power consumption if you know you are not going to use such memory block for some time."}]}]}]]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":14,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"In register "},{"t":"reg","v":"SYSCON_MEM_POWER_UP_REG"},{"t":"text","v":":"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":15,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"By default, all memory enters low-power state when the chip enters the Light-sleep mode."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":16,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Setting different bits of the "},{"t":"field","v":"SYSCON_ROM_POWER_UP"},{"t":"text","v":" field forces different blocks of Internal ROM 0 and Internal ROM 1 to work as normal (do not enter the retention state) when the chip enters Light-sleep."}],"warn":true}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":17,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Setting different bits of the "},{"t":"field","v":"SYSCON_SRAM_POWER_UP"},{"t":"text","v":" field forces different blocks of Internal SRAM to work as normal (do not enter the retention state) when the chip enters Light-sleep."}],"warn":true}]}]]}]]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":18,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For detailed information about the controlling bits of different blocks, please see Table 17.3-1 below."}]}]},{"t":"table","caption":"Table 17.3-1. Internal Memory Controlling Bit","head":[[{"t":"text","v":"Internal Memory"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Lowest Address 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Highest Address 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Lowest Address 2"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Highest Address 2"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Controlling Bit"}]],"rows":[{"n":19,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Internal ROM 0"}],[{"t":"text","v":"0x4000_0000"}],[{"t":"text","v":"0x4003_F